<h1>Disclaimer</h1>
<p>MySpaFilter is an independent reference for hot tub and spa filter cartridges. We are not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by any spa or hot tub manufacturer or any filter brand. That includes Watkins and its Hot Spring, Caldera, Hot Spot and Solana lines, Jacuzzi, Sundance, Bullfrog, Master Spas, Intex, Bestway, Unicel, Pleatco, Filbur, and every other brand named on the site. Brand names, model names and part numbers are trademarks of their respective owners. We use them only to identify a cartridge and the cross-reference the catalogs print.</p>
<h2>What the pages are</h2>
<p>Cartridge pages line up an OEM part number with the Unicel, Pleatco and Filbur numbers cited for it, plus diameter, length and end fittings from those catalogs. Guides summarize the same documents, plus manufacturer owner’s manuals and, where a guide discusses germs or chemical handling, CDC or CPSC pages. The <a href="/data/">dataset</a> is that table in a form you can download. The <a href="/about/#methodology">methodology</a> is the rule: we do not type a number that is not in a cited source, and we mark a row unverified when the sources are thin or they conflict.</p>
<p>A cross-reference is the filter catalog’s statement that its part matches the OEM part’s size and fittings. It is not the spa maker’s statement that an aftermarket cartridge satisfies a warranty. Hot Spring’s maintenance page tells owners to use genuine Watkins filters. Jacuzzi recommends a filter designed for the model. Read your warranty and your owner’s manual before you substitute a part. We are not a spa dealer, a filter manufacturer or a licensed technician, and the byline on the guides is the MySpaFilter Editorial Team, not an individual credential.</p>
<h2>What you should verify</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Fit.</strong> Compare the new cartridge with the one you removed: diameter, overall length, and the top and bottom (open hole, handle, male slip, or thread). Two cartridges with the same diameter and length can still be different parts. The <a href="/guides/open-end-vs-threaded-hot-tub-filters/">fitting guide</a> and the <a href="/guide/">measuring guide</a> are the procedures. The size lookup is a shortlist, not a guarantee.</li>
<li><strong>Count.</strong> Some housings hold two or three cartridges, or a pleated cartridge plus a disposable insert. A two-pack in a box is not automatically the number the spa holds. See <a href="/guides/spas-that-use-more-than-one-filter/">spas that use more than one filter</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Catalog disagreements.</strong> When Unicel, Pleatco and Filbur print different areas or lengths for one OEM number, the cartridge page says so. We do not pick a winner. Measure.</li>
<li><strong>Water care and repairs.</strong> Guides that mention chlorine, bromine, pH, acid soaks or flow-error codes are summarizing the cited page. They are not instructions to ignore the label on a chemical bottle or to open a heater. If a flow error remains after a clean filter and a correct water level, the manufacturer documents tell you to call a dealer.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Retailer links</h2>
<p>Some pages link to Amazon, FiltersFast or Doheny's. Those links can earn us a commission at no extra cost to you. They do not change which cartridges we list. Amazon links use this site’s Associates tag and <code>rel="sponsored nofollow noopener"</code>. Direct product links are used only after the listing title was checked; otherwise the button is a search. We do not publish prices or star ratings, because they change and we have not reviewed products in a lab. Details are on the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>. The purchase, the return and the listing contents are between you and the retailer.</p>
<h2>No warranty</h2>
<p>Information is provided as-is, for general information, with no warranty of any kind. Manufacturers revise catalogs and supersede part numbers. A page can be wrong, and a source can be wrong. If you find a part number, a dimension or a sentence that the cited document does not support, email <a href="mailto:contact@myspafilter.com">contact@myspafilter.com</a> or use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. The corrections policy is on the <a href="/about/#corrections">about page</a>. To the extent the law allows, MySpaFilter is not liable for a purchase, a repair or a water-care decision you make from these pages. The <a href="/terms/">terms of use</a> state that limit in contract language.</p>
